{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"5c857bd39e6805c0","name":"card_event_protect_the_pocket","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/BrothersInArms/events/card_event_protect_the_pocket","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"PROTECT THE POCKET","text":"Draw 4 cards. If you have 4+ units with active Pincer, end the next enemy turn immediately.","flavorText":"In military context, the term \"pocket\" is often used to describe a situation where a group of enemy forces become encircled and cut off from their main force, or are trapped in a confined geographic area, often resulting in their capture or defeat. For example, in 1944, the Allied forces in Europe were able to create a pocket around German forces in the Falaise region of Normandy, France, by encircling them and preventing them from escaping. Earlier Hitler had refused to allow the German forces to withdraw and instead ordered him to conduct Operation Lüttich, a counter-offensive at Mortain against the US. Despite objections from his generals, Hitler insisted on the attack, but the four depleted panzer divisions involved were insufficient to defeat the Allied armies. As a result, the Germans were driven deeper into the Allied envelopment, ultimately leading to their defeat  The battle of the Falaise pocket resulted in the destruction of most of the German Army Group B west of the Seine, which opened the way to Paris and the Franco-German border.","faction":"Germany","type":"order","rarity":"Rare","cost":10,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_protect_the_pocket","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_protect_the_pocket_title","SourceString":"PROTECT THE POCKET","LocalizedString":"PROTECT THE POCKET"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":10,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_protect_the_pocket_text","SourceString":"Draw 4 cards. If you have 4+ units with active Pincer, end the next enemy turn immediately.","LocalizedString":"Draw 4 cards. If you have 4+ units with active Pincer, end the next enemy turn immediately."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_protect_the_pocket_history","SourceString":"In military context, the term \"pocket\" is often used to describe a situation where a group of enemy forces become encircled and cut off from their main force, or are trapped in a confined geographic area, often resulting in their capture or defeat. For example, in 1944, the Allied forces in Europe were able to create a pocket around German forces in the Falaise region of Normandy, France, by encircling them and preventing them from escaping. Earlier Hitler had refused to allow the German forces to withdraw and instead ordered him to conduct Operation Lüttich, a counter-offensive at Mortain against the US. Despite objections from his generals, Hitler insisted on the attack, but the four depleted panzer divisions involved were insufficient to defeat the Allied armies. As a result, the Germans were driven deeper into the Allied envelopment, ultimately leading to their defeat  The battle of the Falaise pocket resulted in the destruction of most of the German Army Group B west of the Seine, which opened the way to Paris and the Franco-German border.","LocalizedString":"In military context, the term \"pocket\" is often used to describe a situation where a group of enemy forces become encircled and cut off from their main force, or are trapped in a confined geographic area, often resulting in their capture or defeat. For example, in 1944, the Allied forces in Europe were able to create a pocket around German forces in the Falaise region of Normandy, France, by encircling them and preventing them from escaping. Earlier Hitler had refused to allow the German forces to withdraw and instead ordered him to conduct Operation Lüttich, a counter-offensive at Mortain against the US. Despite objections from his generals, Hitler insisted on the attack, but the four depleted panzer divisions involved were insufficient to defeat the Allied armies. As a result, the Germans were driven deeper into the Allied envelopment, ultimately leading to their defeat  The battle of the Falaise pocket resulted in the destruction of most of the German Army Group B west of the Seine, which opened the way to Paris and the Franco-German border."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BrothersInArms","isReserved":true,"usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnStartofTurn"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Germany/Spring2023Candidates/t_protect_the_pocket.t_protect_the_pocket","SubPathString":""},"artist":"German WWII Magazine","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/PROTECT_THE_POCKET.PROTECT_THE_POCKET","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":341.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_protect_the_pocket_photo","SourceString":"Camouflaged German armored vehicles in a village in France, 1944.","LocalizedString":"Camouflaged German armored vehicles in a village in France, 1944."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""}},"variables":[{"name":"count","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"ExecuteUbergraph_card_event_protect_the_pocket","owner":"card_event_protect_the_pocket_C","params":[{"name":"EntryPoint","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"pure":false,"event":false,"flags":"FUNC_Final | FUNC_UbergraphFunction | FUNC_HasDefaults","locals":[{"name":"Temp_int_Array_Index_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"Temp_int_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"K2Node_Event_targetCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*",